                  <h3>ZIP first=3F</h3>=0A<p>I love ideas that feel clearly=
 better than what was before. I used to feel that way about curved shower c=
urtain bars. Like, instead of the shower curtain being perfectly straight a=
gainst the edge of the shower, it curves outward. No harm in functionality,=
 but it gives more space inside the shower. It=E2=80=99s just better. There=
 are more factors, though, sadly. Surely they are harder to manufacture, pa=
ckage, and ship, and thus more expensive. Maybe you need longer shower curt=
ains, too=3F Maybe there isn=E2=80=99t always space for it in smaller bathr=
ooms=3F I still generally prefer it when possible. It=E2=80=99s an optional=
 improvement.</p>=0A<p>Here=E2=80=99s another thing like that: <a href=3D"h=
ttps://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/5RfLBS-dqLGF-QFUCXP3Nw~~/AABEfhA~/6bK0lD8Z=
9RYS5957eyj-rDo3XBLe25rk1lA5GQ42LtJ5bKX0cqK8sptiQoMMabR8sbSw5tju2LkJhW6xiV5=
hK-XHcoYn97mp5eJs819yrcpLBjobWQQLOohvyJk3ZZT3">Put the ZIP code first</a>.<=
/p>=0A<p>The big idea is that we should ask for the ZIP code in an address =
first, not last. Here=E2=80=99s what address forms often look like:</p>=0A<=
img src=3D"https://production-codepen-email-assets.codepenassets.com/cdn-cg=
i/image/width=3D600,quality=3D90,format=3Dauto/codepen-spark/address_form_s=
park508.png" alt=3D"A typical shipping address form with fields for the rec=
ipient's name and mailing address. " width=3D"450"/>=0A<p>ZIP code is 2nd t=
o last there. Notably, before the City. But if we asked for the ZIP code fi=
rst, the city would just be implied, saving time filling out the form. Time=
 saved during e-commerce checkouts is a proven way to improve conversion ra=
tes.</p>=0A<p>As that microsite says:</p>=0A<blockquote><p>From those 5 cha=
racters you can determine the city, the state, and the country. That=E2=80=
=99s 3 fields. Autofilled. From one input.</p></blockquote>=0A<p>That=E2=80=
=99s just better, right=3F</p>=0A<p>Seems better to me, but I bet there are=
 more factors. For one, it=E2=80=99s <em>different</em>, and different migh=
t feel weird to users and throw them off, maybe not saving time at all. Peo=
ple have addresses in their head in a certain way/order, and matching that =
might have its own benefit.</p>=0A<p>For another, this requires extra code =
to work. You need some kind of reliable and updated ZIP code matching softw=
are. Extra notably, the demo on that page <em>doesn=E2=80=99t even work.</e=
m> I get a 404 for the API they are using:</p>=0A<img src=3D"https://produc=
tion-codepen-email-assets.codepenassets.com/cdn-cgi/image/width=3D600,quali=
ty=3D90,format=3Dauto/codepen-spark/404_error_508.png" alt=3D"404 error in =
the header for the API zippopatam" width=3D"400"/>=0A<p>Also, and this I kn=
ow is true, but I am ignorant about the details: <strong>ZIP codes are weir=
d</strong>. They have different formats and aren=E2=80=99t necessarily glob=
ally unique. So asking for the country first is actually probably best, eve=
n if that=E2=80=99s one of the most painful parts of address forms.</p>=0A<=
p>Still, maybe it=E2=80=99s an improvement! Maybe try it!</p>=0A<p>Ya know =
that screenshot from above=3F That=E2=80=99s actually from Stripe Elements,=
 which is super incentivized to make payment forms that convert well. This =
is what they actually do by default (<a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.c=
om/f/a/xdplq7TOl68GM3FvwmFwTA~~/AABEfhA~/H6SCZVjHcQ9yTu1w3OLPgIslsY1vqabM2X=
PxrwrXd0Carojvrc1GuWuq1uMhrJyrAObvEvU-3mBGwyOc_lmg-Q8ZUeirqQPYwOEobovuWp63F=
wqcsevsA5hAz1l96v-ogOgKz3Ds9APMaYuFYxea0g~~">in their own demo</a>):</p>=0A=
<img src=3D"https://production-codepen-email-assets.codepenassets.com/cdn-c=
gi/image/width=3D600,quality=3D90,format=3Dauto/codepen-spark/stripe_elemen=
ts_demo_508.png" alt=3D"A shipping address form from Stripe Elements. " wid=
th=3D"300"/>=0A<p>Me, I=E2=80=99d think that Address field would be full of=
 magic. You could drop in the ZIP code and it would prefill stuff. Or you c=
ould single-line type your entire address and it would just know what you m=
ean and deal with it. But no, actually, that=E2=80=99s just what it wants f=
or your street address line, and if you fill it out and press Enter or Tab,=
 it expands to show you all the fields it actually needs. Weird.</p>=0A<p>T=
he more magic at helping me fill out forms, the better really. Make them ac=
cessible. Use all the <a href=3D"https://go.sparkpostmail2.com/f/a/N_zfQZEO=
vWGV0itgT3az3A~~/AABEfhA~/Wbxs4zUH1eCtRoDpTF3ve0bnYPcb19VGm0ZDIn0lmOhC-Jb8j=
HR0jjd2FIYjPhoc8VU4MLY-zxE8wl5HLri_fcYQCgQeLTIeG4VdpQWlNAjROcMPh96PEcyJQvJD=
S_4M">fancy attributes</a> to make them more understandable for tools and i=
mprove UX. Do fancy backend processing. Use the geolocation API. Whatever. =
Nobody loves filling out forms, they love what the form helps them do.</p>=
